        }
      ],
      "content": "Sloeland Farmhouse 1. 967 (formerly listed as Sloughland Farmhouse) SP 90 SE 5/107            10.11.51. II           GV 2. C16 main block, C17 south west wing at back, early to mid C19 front wall and slightly heightened roof,  Red bricks, Welsh slates.  Timber framework of main structure visible on side elevation.  2 storeys, bracketed eaves cornice. 4 1st floor sashes, ground floor French windows and canted bay on left.  South west wing of red brick and timber framework, 2 storeys, casements. Sloeland Farmhouse, granary and barn form a group. Listing NGR: SP9679303782"
    }
